    "created_at": "2016-02-25T13:54:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-26T17:49:24Z",
    "body": "> Hmm. I don't think that interpretation is supported by the spec at all. So if I addEventListener on the <i>, it will never be called?\n\nRight. The spec doesn't define hit testing. And in Gecko hit testing here happens to catch `<button>` and not `<i>` here.\n",
